meta {
  name: List ASH exit records
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/forms/ash/exit?page=&limit=&orderBy=&search=&sortBy=
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  page: 
  limit: 
  orderBy: 
  search: 
  sortBy: 
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # List ASH Exit Records
  
  Returns a paginated list of ASH exit records, ordered by creation date. Supports full-text search via PostgreSQL GIN index.
  
  ## Authorization
  Requires `read` permission.
  
  ## Query Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type   | Required | Default     | Description / Allowed Values                                                                                          |
  |-----------|--------|----------|-------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | page      | number | No       | `1`         | Page number (integer ≥ 1)                                                                                             |
  | limit     | number | No       | `25`        | Items per page (integer, 1–100)                                                                                       |
  | orderBy   | string | No       | `desc`      | Sort direction. One of: `asc`, `desc`                                                                                 |
  | sortBy    | string | No       | `createdAt` | One of: `ageAtExit`, `schoolName`, `classAtExit`, `durationInProgram`, `facilitatorName`, `exitDate`, `createdAt`      |
  | search    | string | No       | —           | Full-text search query. When provided, cache and sort filters are bypassed and results are matched against the GIN index. |
  
  ### Searchable Fields
  
  | Field                | Weight | Notes                                          |
  |----------------------|--------|-------------------------------------------------|
  | `schoolName`         | A      | Combined with `firstName` + `surname` from the joined ASH student record |
  | `firstName`          | A      | From the joined ASH student record              |
  | `surname`            | A      | From the joined ASH student record              |
  | `classAtExit`        | B      |                                                 |
  | `durationInProgram`  | B      |                                                 |
  | `exitReason`         | C      |                                                 |
  | `areasOfImprovement` | C      |                                                 |
  
  ## Response
  
  **`200 OK`** — Returns a paginated array of ASH exit records. Each item includes `firstName` and `surname` from the joined ASH student record.
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": [
      {
        "firstName": "string",
        "surname": "string",
        "id": "uuid",
        "studentId": "uuid",
        "ageAtExit": 14,
        "schoolName": "string",
        "classAtExit": "string",
        "durationInProgram": "string",
        "exitReason": "string",
        "academicImpactRating": 7,
        "areasOfImprovement": ["string"] | null,
        "mentorshipReceived": "string",
        "mentorshipImpactRating": 8 | null,
        "postAshStatus": "string",
        "institutionName": "string" | null,
        "courseOfStudy": "string" | null,
        "vocationalSkill": "string" | null,
        "enjoyedMost": "string" | null,
        "programImpact": "string" | null,
        "improvementSuggestions": "string" | null,
        "facilitatorName": "string",
        "exitDate": "YYYY-MM-DD",
        "updatedAt": "ISO 8601" | null,
        "createdAt": "ISO 8601",
        "deletedAt": "ISO 8601" | null
      }
    ],
    "meta": {
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 25,
        "totalPages": 1
      },
      "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Errors
  
  | Status                      | Description                                         |
  |-----------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
  | `400 Bad Request`           | Invalid query parameters (e.g. non-numeric `page`). |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.                            |
}
